IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hca-dates`
IMPORT `hca-rules`
IMPORT `hca-seat`

-- Health Complaints Act 2016 (Vic) -- worked cases for the complainant's questions (hca-seat.l4), the date helpers
-- (hca-dates.l4) and the shared rules (hca-rules.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text;
-- none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the
-- law. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`me` MEANS `the person who received or sought the service`
`other` MEANS `another person`
`carer` MEANS `a carer of the person who received or sought the service`
`any day` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

§§ `Dates`

-- 12 months after 29 February 2028 is 28 February 2029 (no 29th: last day, fork F2); 3 months after 30 November 2026 is
-- 28 February 2027; 6 months after 31 August 2027 is 29 February 2028; 84 days after 1 March 2027 is 24 May 2027 (30
-- days to 31 March, 30 in April, 24 in May); 28 days after 15 January 2027 is 12 February 2027.
#ASSERT `the date` 12 `months after` (`d` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2029
#ASSERT `the date` 3 `months after` (`d` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the date` 84 `days after` (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 24 5 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 28 `days after` (`d` 15 1 2027) EQUALS `d` 12 2 2027

§§ `s 3 -- health service, general health service, party`

#ASSERT `Was it a health service` `an activity to assess, maintain or improve health, or to diagnose, prevent or treat illness, injury or disability` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it a health service` `therapeutic counselling or psychotherapy` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it a health service` `a service prescribed by the regulations` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it a health service` `none of these` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- (i) ancillary services need both limbs.
#ASSERT `Was it a health service` `an ancillary service such as laundry, cleaning or catering` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it a health service` `an ancillary service such as laundry, cleaning or catering` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- A naturopath, unregistered: general. A registered physiotherapist practising physiotherapy: not general. Nothing: not.
#ASSERT `Was it a general health service` `an activity to assess, maintain or improve health, or to diagnose, prevent or treat illness, injury or disability` FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Was it a general health service` `an activity to assess, maintain or improve health, or to diagnose, prevent or treat illness, injury or disability` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Was it a general health service` `none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Party: s 3, s 22.
#ASSERT `Am I a party to the complaint` `the complainant` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a party to the complaint` `the health service provider complained about` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a party to the complaint` `the person who received or sought the service, not the complainant` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a party to the complaint` `the person who received or sought the service, not the complainant` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a party to the complaint` `someone else` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `ss 5(1), 6(1), 7(1) -- complaining to the provider`

-- Arguments: who, unreasonable provision, failure to provide, principles, manner, candour, my complaint's handling, the
-- patient's complaint's handling, carer treated, carer treated over candour.
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the provider` `me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the provider` `me` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the provider` `me` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 5(1) has no head for another's complaint or for treatment of a carer.
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the provider` `me` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the provider` `me` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6(1)(e)(ii): another person about the handling of the patient's complaint.
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the provider` `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the provider` `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the provider` `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 7(1)(a), (ab); and a carer under s 6 about the service to the person cared for (fork F3).
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the provider` `carer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the provider` `carer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the provider` `carer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the provider` `another person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 5(2), 6(2), 7(2), 8 -- complaining to the Commissioner`

-- Arguments: who; the nine heads as above; code or order breach; unreasonable to go to the provider first; complained to
-- the provider; the day; resolved; the day resolved; service provided; day completed; day sought; today; Commissioner
-- satisfied to deal with it late.
`yes` MEANS `yes, you may complain to the Commissioner`
`late but taken` MEANS `out of time, but the Commissioner is satisfied the circumstances require it and may deal with it (s 8(2))`
`too late` MEANS `no, it is more than 12 months after the service (s 8(1))`
`no route` MEANS `not yet on these facts: the Act gives no route to the Commissioner`

-- (a) straight to the Commissioner; service completed 1 March 2027, last day 1 March 2028.
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) `any day` (`d` 1 3 2028) FALSE EQUALS `yes`
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) `any day` (`d` 2 3 2028) FALSE EQUALS `too late`
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) `any day` (`d` 2 3 2028) TRUE EQUALS `late but taken`
-- Not unreasonable to go to the provider, and not yet complained to it: no route.
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) `any day` (`d` 1 4 2027) FALSE EQUALS `no route`
-- (c) complained to the provider on 30 November 2026; the 3 months end on 28 February 2027 (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 11 2026) `any day` (`d` 28 2 2027) FALSE EQUALS `no route`
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 11 2026) `any day` (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `yes`
-- Resolved on 15 February 2027, within the 3 months: no route by (c). Resolved on 1 March 2027, after them: route.
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 2 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 11 2026) `any day` (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `no route`
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 11 2026) `any day` (`d` 2 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `yes`
-- (b) a code breach by a general provider, from another person, straight to the Commissioner.
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) `any day` (`d` 1 4 2027) FALSE EQUALS `yes`
-- (b) for a carer, through s 6(2) (fork F3).
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `carer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) `any day` (`d` 1 4 2027) FALSE EQUALS `yes`
-- (d) the provider's handling of my complaint, two weeks after making it.
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `me` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2027) FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 12 2026) `any day` (`d` 15 1 2027) FALSE EQUALS `yes`
-- s 8(1)(b): sought 10 June 2027 and not provided; last day 10 June 2028.
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 10 6 2027) (`d` 10 6 2028) FALSE EQUALS `yes`
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `me` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 10 6 2027) (`d` 11 6 2028) FALSE EQUALS `too late`
-- Leap day: completed 29 February 2028; last day 28 February 2029.
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 29 2 2028) `any day` (`d` 28 2 2029) FALSE EQUALS `yes`
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 29 2 2028) `any day` (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE EQUALS `too late`
-- Finding 5: the provider route uses up the 12 months. Completed 1 January 2027; complained to the provider 15 December
-- 2027; unresolved on 16 March 2028 (3 months ended 15 March 2028): route (c) open, but s 8(1) passed on 1 January 2028.
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 12 2027) FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 1 2027) `any day` (`d` 16 3 2028) FALSE EQUALS `too late`
#ASSERT `Can I complain to the Commissioner` `me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 12 2027) FALSE `any day` TRUE (`d` 1 1 2027) `any day` (`d` 16 3 2028) TRUE EQUALS `late but taken`

