#ASSERT `Can the conciliation be used in court` `an undertaking the provider gave the Commissioner` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `What must I be given at the end of the process` TRUE `not yet decided` EQUALS `a copy of the written record of the agreement (s 38(1))`
#ASSERT `What must I be given at the end of the process` FALSE `to take no further action` EQUALS `written notice of the reasons for taking no further action (s 38(4))`
#ASSERT `What must I be given at the end of the process` FALSE `to investigate` EQUALS `written notice of the investigation, with the formal description of the complaint (s 49)`
#ASSERT `What must I be given at the end of the process` FALSE `not yet decided` EQUALS `nothing yet: the Commissioner has not decided what follows (s 38(3))`

#ASSERT `Must I be told the conciliation outcome` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I be told the conciliation outcome` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

